1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,271
A Small Apology.

3
00:00:03,271 --> 00:00:05,719
Emma lends me her favorite comic book.

4
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:08,833
I put it on my desk, right beside a cup of water.

5
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:11,333
You can probably guess what happens next.

6
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:15,375
My elbow moves, the cup tips, and the corner of the cover gets wet.

7
00:00:15,652 --> 00:00:16,635
Oh.

8
00:00:16,635 --> 00:00:18,333
That doesn't look good.

9
00:00:18,604 --> 00:00:20,348
No, it doesn't.

10
00:00:20,348 --> 00:00:24,723
I move the cup, gently dry the book, and leave it open where it won't get knocked again.

11
00:00:24,723 --> 00:00:26,681
The corner still looks bent.

12
00:00:26,681 --> 00:00:29,744
For a minute, I wish I could pretend it was always like that.

13
00:00:30,028 --> 00:00:31,749
Are you going to tell Emma?

14
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:33,132
Yes.

15
00:00:33,132 --> 00:00:35,664
I just need to stop being nervous first.

16
00:00:35,664 --> 00:00:38,914
The next day, I give her the book and explain what happened.

17
00:00:38,914 --> 00:00:40,570
I'm really sorry.

18
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,476
I should have been more careful.

19
00:00:42,698 --> 00:00:43,856
Thanks for telling me.

20
00:00:43,856 --> 00:00:45,325
I am disappointed, though.

21
00:00:45,325 --> 00:00:46,752
I really like this book.

22
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,191
I know.

23
00:00:48,191 --> 00:00:49,805
What can I do to help?

24
00:00:49,805 --> 00:00:52,410
I can replace it with my allowance if you'd like.

25
00:00:52,634 --> 00:00:54,761
Let me see how it looks when it's fully dry.

26
00:00:54,761 --> 00:00:56,532
Maybe we can flatten the corner.

27
00:00:56,532 --> 00:00:58,511
I'll tell you if I want a replacement.

28
00:00:58,780 --> 00:00:59,909
Okay.

29
00:00:59,909 --> 00:01:02,638
I won't try to fix anything else without asking.

30
00:01:02,638 --> 00:01:04,586
We sit together at lunch.

31
00:01:04,586 --> 00:01:09,305
It feels a little awkward at first, but then Emma starts talking about the next book in the series.

32
00:01:09,305 --> 00:01:12,180
At home that afternoon, Ben wants an update.

33
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,139
Are you still friends?

34
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,540
Yes.

35
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,342
Friends can be disappointed and still be friends.

36
00:01:18,342 --> 00:01:21,801
Also, all future cups of water are getting their own table.

37
00:01:21,801 --> 00:01:24,009
Far away from the comic books.
